/-!
# Self-balanced product towers at `(n, k) = (7, 8)` over `Z/2`

Four functions on matchings of `ontoFPHP 7 8`, each an `m`-block product (`ProdM.bal_prodM`) of
locally balanced blocks, hence balanced against itself at every level `e ≤ 3`:

* `RBd`: a `2 × 2` rectangle tower (pigeons `12, 13`, holes `4, 5`) ⊗ K167's `B` on pigeons `< 12`
  × holes `< 4` (via `HDes.B7`, local levels `≤ 2`) ⊗ the pin `(14, 6)`. On edges it is the
  rectangle; it vanishes at `[]`.
* `TB`: the `3 × 3` tower of `T` (pigeons `12..14`, holes `4..6`) ⊗ `B`.
* `RRM`: rectangles on `{0,1} × {0,1}` and `{2,3} × {2,3}` ⊗ an explicit local unit design `M` of
  degree 2 on pigeons `4..14` × holes `4..6` (`M [] = 1`, odd on the edges `S1`, odd on the pairs
  `S2`; generated by agents/pr/work/py3/m113.py).
* `RRRM`: rectangles on `{0,1}², {2,3}², {4,5}²` ⊗ the all-ones `9 × 1` block (pigeons `6..14`, hole 6).

Block towers: rectangle `lf [s ≥ 1]`, `T` `lf [s ≥ 2]`, pin and `9 × 1` block `lf 1` (`LocLf`).
-/

